    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the entire test suite passes (39 tests, 0 failures/errors), including all the duplicate-detection checkpoints.\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated all create-owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, rejecting with **409 only on a whole-key match**.\n\n**New code**\n- `IdentityKeys` (common) \u2014 derives the key from an owner's stored telephone/email/householdId; single source used by both the mapper and the reject step.\n- `Households` (owner package) \u2014 extracted the household-matching + stable `householdId` hash logic so the reject step and `AssignHousehold` compute the *same* household id (no drift).\n- `RejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 the one duplicate step. It resolves the request's would-be `householdId` (same logic `AssignHousehold` will apply), builds the candidate key, and 409s only if it exactly equals an existing owner's key.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML (returns 409 Conflict).\n\n**Changes**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema (so it's generated into `OwnerDto` and returned).\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 maps `identityKey` via `IdentityKeys.of(owner)`.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 replaced the three steps (`rejectDuplicateTelephone` \u2192 `rejectDuplicateEmail` \u2192 `rejectDuplicateHousehold`) with a single `rejectDuplicateIdentity`.\n- `AssignHousehold` \u2014 now delegates to `Households`.\n\n**Removed** the three old reject functions, their exceptions, handlers, and escalation YAMLs (no dangling references remain).\n\n**Behaviour change, as specified:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are **both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The old separate telephone/email/household 409s are now expressed purely through this one key.\n\nNote: the reject runs before the owner is built (matching the existing \"validate-early\" pipeline order), so it computes the candidate's household component up front via the shared `Households.resolve` rather than relying on the later `AssignHousehold` mutation \u2014 keeping detection side-effect-free.",
